 I was still functioning  though and just about got my problem  sheets in though I seriously struggled  to see my day in the life video for  example and I applied for some phd's I  was offered places at Oxford and reading  and I was over the moon to accept my  place at Oxford with a three year  scholarship or real dependent on me  getting a 2:1 or above at my degree I  was riding on a good t1 and I felt  confident no matter what happened I  should still get one overall however my  depression was starting to get out of  control in the run-up to my exams I  found myself locking myself in cupboards  in the library and just crying sometimes  for over an hour I just didn't know what  to do I couldn't understand what was  happening to me it all culminated when a  few days before my exams I had a  full-blown panic attack at first I  thought it was a heart attack but upon  googling symptoms of panic attack I  realized what was going on it seriously  shoot me up I genuinely felt like  knowledge had tumbled out of my head and  it made me feel like crap the logical  thing to do here of course would have  been to tell someone and asked to defer  my exams maybe it was obvious that I was  in no fit state to do them but I didn't  I hinted to a few friends that I was  struggling and I just carried on I was  just too proud to ask for help the days  before I finished my exams were the  darkest of my life I barely slept I  worked all day on things I didn't  understand and I started to hate myself  so much that I would cut myself it was  horrible but I did it and I not sure why  of course I did terribly in my exams but  passed them both which meant that I  still got a degree now the requirement  to get a 2:1 is to achieve 59.5% average  overall what I got was fifty nine point  four five percent my PhD supervisor told  me that she didn't care and  she would take musical Department to get  me my scholarship anyway but they flatly  refused and they pulled my funding I  later found out that she was absolutely  furious about this and made a formal  complaint to the University by the  biggest stroke of luck possible though  while this was all happening she was at  a conference and she mentioned to a  colleague the situation this colleague  had a career integration grant from the  EU and could take on PhD students while  he was in the math department at Exeter  we exchanged emails a college okayed it  and I got my Blaise here from this point  everything started looking up I moved  down to Exeter and I threw myself into  student life I took courses on advanced  maths and I started doing some original  if for now guided research I started  lifting weights seriously and I got  myself in shape I joined the a capella  Society because I thought that one of  the musical directors was fit and knew  lots about gaming and we've been going  out ever since I've been busy around the  clock with so many different things and  I'm incredibly lucky to have the friends  I have I moved into a house with three  guys from the department and I get to  sing almost every day with some of the  best people I know including my  girlfriend but there's a big element of  this story missing what about YouTube I  hear you cry when I applied to Oxford I  try to find out information about  student life by all possible means and  one of the things I did was of course to  search on YouTube but I turned up  nothing at that time only the side  business school had a channel instead  the most useful thing I found was  talking very briefly and buyer emailed  someone who did physics VAR a mutual  friend the personal honest depiction of  student life really reassured me and I  meant I had no qualms at all about  accepting my offer after spending a few  months at Oxford I realized that I had a  really valuable perspective not just as  somebody on the course but also having  talked to the Masons choosers so I made  a video I use my terrible 4 megapixel  camera and I edited it on that machine  at the university computing department  because I didn't own any editing  software I uploaded it to my channel and  I watched as its fuse crapped up one by  one when I hit a hundred views I was so  happy I thought I'd really hit it big so  I decided to make more videos seeing  that people were benefiting from the  first one and I went for my interview  questions and I did a Q&amp;A and an FAQ in  the video and studying and people  somehow kept watching eventually I went  to some Peters and said that they should  make a YouTube channel because what I  was doing was working and they said ok  you make it  I did originally it was only gonna be  interviews with a few people that on a  student perspective I talked about but  it seemed grew into something much  bigger it went live in 2011 and it  changed how many colleges dealer access  work building on its success and trying  to find something to do with myself my  fourth year I hit on the idea of making  weekly vlogs to give an honest student  perspective on Oxford life and the Oxbow  project was born it started slowly but  especially after I was joined by Jamie  aka Jamie Mills it grew in size and by  the year's end it amassed hundreds and  thousands of fans  I pushed the university to continue the  project the next year is a collaboration  between undergraduates from across the  university but there wasn't much  interest so I created a channel myself  and I recruited five amazing students he  went on to get over a hundred thousand  views and a devoted following this year  we have six students who will take the  project even further and I'm confident  they're going to blaze a trail at  universities across the world will  follow so now I'm at an interesting  crossroads I've always imagined that I  would finish my PhD I do a postdoc and I  continue down that path as an academic  but not on so much media production  hundreds of videos all told as well as  radio and journalism I find myself drawn  down another path the idea of producing  scientific video content whether in an  online format like scishow or crash  course or on TV is a very appealing one  after my doctorate I will need to make a  choice to go in on one path or the other  and right now I honestly don't know  which I'll choose maybe I'll go down a  third path I've been increasingly  thinking about maybe directing a short  film these days I'm at a really exciting  position in my life where I have an  awful lot of opportunities presented to  me and I'm incredibly grateful for this  amazing online community which has  sprung up around the videos which I've  done and I know no matter what I choose  to do the future will support and be  there for me
 

